# Signing material. Nothing in this repo needs a keystore checked in: the release build is
# unsigned and CI reads credentials from the environment (see README, "Signing").
# If you ever add a local debug keystore, it must never reach a commit.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.der
*.cer
*.crt
*.mobileprovision
google-services.json

# Local SDK/IDE paths and machine state
local.properties
.idea
.kotlin
*.hprof.hs_err_pid*

# Tool-generated indexes. `.codegraph/` is a 9 MB SQLite graph rebuilt from the source tree;
# it is a local cache, not source, and would be several MB of churn on every commit.
.codegraph

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.trash/
.Trash-*/
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.Trash-*/
# Windows recycle bin and macOS trash: local samples have been recovered from these before,
# and this project deliberately never pulls media back out of them.
*_RECYCLE.BIN/

# NOTE: `samples/` is intentionally NOT ignored.
# The JPEG and MP4 fixtures under `samples/` are committed on purpose: they are what let the
# test suite verify per-vendor motion-photo detection offline, and stripping them would turn
# 332 passing assertions into a pile of skips.
#
# Before committing any sample, note that real camera files carry EXIF. Coordinates were removed
# from the committed fixtures, but **check any newly added file**: strip GPS (IFD tag 0x8825),
# the `©xyz` MP4 atom, and Artist/Copyright/ImageDescription before adding it. See
# `tools/strip-sample-metadata.py`, which does this without moving a single byte — rewriting a
# TIFF structure would invalidate the absolute offsets inside vendor MakerNotes, and the vendor
# detection tests would stop passing for reasons that look like a code bug.
#
# `samples/.DS_Store` is ignored below for the same reason it is ignored everywhere: it is
# Finder's idea of what belongs in a directory.
samples/.DS_Store

# Scratch space for the verification harness (samples' derived output, ffprobe dumps, etc.)
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.log